{"version":3,"term":{"cols":108,"rows":48},"timestamp":1792510025,"command":"bash -c 'printf \"$ python3 bench/demo.py\\n\"; sleep 1; python3 bench/demo.py --pace 1.2 --bin bench/.cache/build-worktree-Release/server; sleep 3'","title":"Fault-Tolerant KV Store live demo","env":{"SHELL":"/bin/zsh"}}
[0.010, "o", "$ python3 bench/demo.py\r\n"]
[1.114, "o", "\u001b[1mFault-Tolerant KV Store — live demo\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.203, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m[1/8] Leader election\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    Start 5 server processes. Each waits a random 300-500 ms, then campaigns for votes.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.361, "o", "    \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m node 2 (127.0.0.1:19002) won the election in 361 ms\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "    cluster: 0:follower  1:follower  \u001b[32m2:LEADER\u001b[0m  3:follower  4:follower\r\n"]
[1.201, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m[2/8] Client redirection\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    Only the leader accepts commands; followers point clients to it.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.002, "o", "    SET greeting hello  →  node 0 (127.0.0.1:19000) replies \u001b[33mNOT_LEADER 127.0.0.1:19002\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "    \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m client followed the redirect; leader replied \u001b[33mOK\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "    \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m GET greeting  →  \u001b[33m\"hello, raft\"\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.201, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m[3/8] Replication\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    A write is acknowledged only after a majority has it; every replica then applies it to its AOF.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.002, "o", "    \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m SET city Lisbon committed in 1.72 ms\r\n"]
[0.130, "o", "    \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m node 0 (127.0.0.1:19000) AOF: city = Lisbon\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "    \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m node 1 (127.0.0.1:19001) AOF: city = Lisbon\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "    \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m node 2 (127.0.0.1:19002) AOF: city = Lisbon\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "    \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m node 3 (127.0.0.1:19003) AOF: city = Lisbon\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "    \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m node 4 (127.0.0.1:19004) AOF: city = Lisbon\r\n"]
[1.200, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m[4/8] Throughput\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    32 concurrent clients doing 50/50 SET/GET for 3 seconds.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.501, "o", "      12,009 ops/s  \u001b[36m████████████████████████\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.500, "o", "      11,724 ops/s  \u001b[36m███████████████████████\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.500, "o", "      11,800 ops/s  \u001b[36m███████████████████████\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.500, "o", "      12,096 ops/s  \u001b[36m████████████████████████\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.500, "o", "      11,704 ops/s  \u001b[36m███████████████████████\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.500, "o", "      11,212 ops/s  \u001b[36m██████████████████████\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.006, "o", "    \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m 35,289 ops in 3 s (11,763 ops/s)  ·  latency p50 2.54 ms, p99 5.06 ms\r\n"]
[1.201, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m[5/8] Leader crash under load\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    16 writers keep writing unique keys while the leader is killed with SIGKILL.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.002, "o", "    \u001b[33m↯\u001b[0m killed node 2 (127.0.0.1:19002) after 7,349 acknowledged writes\r\n"]
[0.449, "o", "    \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m node 0 (127.0.0.1:19000) took over; writes resumed after 447 ms\r\n"]
[1.001, "o", "    cluster: \u001b[32m0:LEADER\u001b[0m  1:follower  \u001b[31m2:down\u001b[0m  3:follower  4:follower\r\n"]
[0.018, "o", "    \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m audit: all 13,924 acknowledged writes present on the new leader — none lost\r\n"]
[1.202, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m[6/8] Surviving a minority of failures\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    A 5-node cluster needs 3 nodes for a majority, so it tolerates 2 failure(s).\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "    \u001b[33m↯\u001b[0m killed node 1 (127.0.0.1:19001)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "    cluster: \u001b[32m0:LEADER\u001b[0m  \u001b[31m1:down\u001b[0m  \u001b[31m2:down\u001b[0m  3:follower  4:follower\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "    \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m with 3/5 nodes up, SET still commits (OK, 4.1 ms)\r\n"]
[1.201, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m[7/8] Losing quorum safely\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    With a majority down, the leader must not acknowledge writes — it can't guarantee durability.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "    \u001b[33m↯\u001b[0m killed node 3 (127.0.0.1:19003)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "    cluster: \u001b[32m0:LEADER\u001b[0m  \u001b[31m1:down\u001b[0m  \u001b[31m2:down\u001b[0m  \u001b[31m3:down\u001b[0m  4:follower\r\n"]
[2.003, "o", "    \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m only 2/5 nodes up: write NOT acknowledged after 2 s (correct)\r\n"]
[1.201, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m[8/8] Recovery and catch-up\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    Restart every crashed node. Each restores its persisted Raft state and fetches only what it missed.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.055, "o", "    restarted node 1 (127.0.0.1:19001)\r\n"]
[0.041, "o", "    restarted node 2 (127.0.0.1:19002)\r\n"]
[0.040, "o", "    restarted node 3 (127.0.0.1:19003)\r\n"]
[0.002, "o", "    \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m quorum restored: writes accepted again after 138 ms (OK)\r\n"]
[0.519, "o", "    \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m all 5 replicas identical (15,527 keys) 569 ms after restart\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "    cluster: \u001b[32m0:LEADER\u001b[0m  1:follower  2:follower  3:follower  4:follower\r\n"]
[0.014, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[32mDemo complete: every guarantee held.\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.025, "x", "0"]
